<title>GERMANY: SAS, Lufthansa launch Cologne-Copenhagen.</title>
<headline>SAS, Lufthansa launch Cologne-Copenhagen.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scandinavian airline SAS said it will start code-share flights with partner Deutsche Lufthansa AG between Cologne and Copenhagen on June 2.</p>
<p>SAS will fly nonstop three times a day with a Fokker-50 between the two cities under its Germany-Scandinavia joint venture with Lufthansa, a company statement said. The number of flights will be reduced at weekends, it added. --Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom. Tel +44 171 542 7706; Fax: 5017</p>
